From fada3562a00e77a4e0a61bd3e1b1942530451244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:30:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] DADAO: clarify isOffsetFoldingLegal perf-tradeoff scope
 (ML-030a review)

Self-review of d10e7bfa25cd flagged that the commit message's 'small
in-range offsets remain cheap' claim only covers offsets that fit the
load/store's own imm12 displacement (roughly [-2048,2047]); mid-range
offsets that would have fit the 18-bit relocation directly (e.g. +5000)
now cost two extra materialization instructions instead of folding for
free, and that scope wasn't disclosed. No behavior change -- comment
only, expanding the isOffsetFoldingLegal doc comment to state the actual
tradeoff boundary explicitly.
---
 llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOISelLowering.h | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOISelLowering.h b/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOISelLowering.h
index 5e300978afc2..63d848f06e45 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOISelLowering.h
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/DADAO/DADAOISelLowering.h
@@ -74,6 +74,23 @@ public:
   // the existing CONST_WYDE/materializeImm64 path and add them in a
   // register. Matches the same choice made by AArch64/RISC-V/MIPS/Sparc for
   // their own HI/LO-style address materialization.
+  //
+  // Trade-off (ML-030a self-review): this is unconditional, not magnitude-
+  // gated, because the hook itself is never told the prospective post-fold
+  // offset (SelectionDAG::FoldSymbolOffset only passes the pre-fold GA).
+  // Offsets that fit the load/store's own imm12 displacement (roughly
+  // [-2048,2047], see the ADDI_RRII threshold in DADAOISelDAGToDAG.cpp's
+  // ISD::Constant handling) still end up folded there for free by an
+  // unrelated addressing-mode combine, and offsets requiring real 18-bit-
+  // or-larger magnitude are correctness-required to take this path. But
+  // *mid-range* offsets that would have fit the 18-bit relocation directly
+  // (e.g. +5000) now cost two extra materialization instructions
+  // (setzw/orw + add) instead of folding for free into RELA_RIII/
+  // ADDI_RBRRII's imm18 operand as they did before this fix. This is the
+  // same correctness-over-code-size choice RISC-V/MIPS/Sparc/AArch64 make
+  // (none of them re-fold a magnitude-safe offset back in either); a
+  // PerformDAGCombine peephole that re-folds when the total is provably
+  // in range would recover it but does not exist yet.
   bool isOffsetFoldingLegal(const GlobalAddressSDNode *GA) const override;
 
 private:
-- 
